# HARD RULE — no hardcoding (if it can be avoided)

From the **start of every session**: do not hardcode values that already have — or should have — a shared token, constant, or helper.

## Prefer shared sources

- **Typography / spacing / chrome:** `apps/mobile/lib/layoutConstants.ts`
- **Colours:** `useFlareColors()` / theme — not one-off hex in screens
- **Shared product copy:** dedicated copy modules / libs — don’t scatter duplicate strings
- **Tables / env / API bases:** existing shared modules (`TABLES`, `EXPO_PUBLIC_*`, etc.)

## If the token is missing

Add it to the shared place first, then use it — especially when the value should match the design system or will be reused.

## Exception

Truly one-off values that cannot sensibly live in shared constants. If unsure, ask Simon.

Also recorded in `apps/mobile/DEV_NOTES.md` (top, with the health/legal hard rule).
